<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03UM">Remark <span data-tag="03UM">7.6.6.16</span>.</a> In the situation of Proposition <a data-tag="03UL" href="/tag/03UL">7.6.6.15</a>, we can replace $(2)$ by either of the following <em>a priori</em> weaker conditions: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(2')$</dt>
<dd><p>
The $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ admits pullbacks. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2'')$</dt>
<dd><p>
The $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ admits equalizers. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
<p> See Corollary <a data-tag="03G2" href="/tag/03G2">7.6.2.42</a> and <a data-tag="03HF" href="/tag/03HF">7.6.4.25</a>. </p>
